# cert-manager — Apply & Verify (pass-offerings internal TLS)

> **State when this doc starts:** cert-manager is installed via Helm and healthy in the `cert-manager` namespace (controller, webhook, cainjector all `1/1 Running`). All six CRDs are present. No Issuer or Certificate resources exist yet.
>
> **Goal of this phase:** create the issuing chain and mint the `pass-offerings` service certificate. This phase stops when the TLS secret exists with correct SANs. App-side TLS enablement is Anuroop's team (see §5).
>
> **Rules for the agent:**
> 1. Apply in the numbered order below. Ordering is a hard requirement, not a preference.
> 2. Do **not** change the CA duration — it's a deliberate decision (5 years).
> 3. Do **not** touch application Helm charts / deployments. This work ends at producing the secret.
> 4. Pin versions; never use `latest`. JFrog is the only registry — no public egress.

