## 7. Renewal — must be handled before it bites (~60 days out)

cert-manager renews automatically and **rewrites the secret**. Running pods do **not** pick this up — servers read the keystore once at startup. A renewed cert changes nothing until the pod restarts.

Pick one and document it:
1. Deploy **Reloader**, annotate the Deployment to restart on secret change.
2. Accept scheduled restarts aligned to cert lifetime.
3. App-level file watching (app team).

This fails silently — no error, the old cert just expires one day.

